# Explicit structural scope editing, provider-free, sequential native journey.
name: Scope review preserves loose files, explicit acceptance and source drift
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 20 Enter / c build inventory | empty
ask: Does the empty scope surface show a deliberate inventory action, with no implied model or scan work?
keys: c
require-live-snap: 30 DRAFT SCOPES | whole-120x36
ask: Is the whole-repository boundary the default, with coverage, source and pending scan-plan work explained?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 15 DRAFT SCOPES | whole-160x48
ask: At 160x48, is the list/detail grid restrained and readable with visible action controls?
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 15 DRAFT SCOPES | whole-96x89
ask: At 96x89, can the operator inspect rationale, context status and recorded source identity?
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 15 DRAFT SCOPES | whole-80x24
ask: At 80x24, do stacked list and detail panels keep the selected boundary and controls understandable?
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 15 DRAFT SCOPES | whole-60x20
ask: At 60x20, is the whole-repository choice still readable with a discoverable paging action?
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 DRAFT SCOPES | whole-40x12
ask: At 40x12, are selection, editing and reading controls usable without overlap?
keys: NPage NPage
live-snap: whole-40x12-paged
ask: Does actual paging expose more boundary evidence without changing selection or starting work?
resize: 120x36
keys: Enter Down Enter
require-live-snap: 15 First scope name | split-name
type: Auth
keys: Tab
type: auth
keys: Tab
type: Rest
keys: Tab
paste-file: @ART/split-paths.txt
live-snap: split-paths
ask: Can the operator enter multiline paths in a named split form while seeing save and field navigation controls?
keys: F2
require-live-snap: 30 r2 | split-result
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART split
ask: Does the split preserve the loose README and produce two reviewed boundaries with no scans?
keys: Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 15 Field 1/1 | rename
keys: C-u
paste-file: @ART/rename.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 r3 | renamed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART renamed
keys: f
require-live-snap: 25 Files 1..1 of 1 | selected-files
ask: Can the operator inspect concrete included files and return without losing boundary selection?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 Boundary: auth | files-closed
keys: a
require-live-snap: 15 Accept exact boundaries | acceptance
ask: Does acceptance disclose inventory limits and remain separate from scan and allowance approval?
keys: Enter End Enter
require-live-snap: 30 ACCEPTED SCOPES | accepted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART accepted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART change-source
keys: Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 15 Field 1/1 | drift-edit
keys: C-u
type: Changed name
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Action stopped | refused-drift
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART drift
ask: Does changed source refuse the edit, preserve the entered draft and leave the accepted revision intact?
keys: Escape
wait: 1
keys: Escape
wait: 1
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 15 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | quit-confirmation
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted-shell
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 30 ACCEPTED SCOPES | restarted-scopes
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: After real exit and no-color restart, are the saved boundaries readable without silently approving changed source or launching work?
keys: Escape
wait: 1
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
